{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ונפש כי תקריב קרבן מנחה", :translit "ve-nefesh ki takriv korban minchah", :gloss "And when a soul brings a meal-offering"} {:he "נפש", :translit "nefesh", :gloss "soul"} {:he "מנחה", :translit "minchah", :gloss "meal-offering"} {:he "לפני ה'", :translit "lifnei Hashem", :gloss "before YHWH"} {:he "בבן בקר", :translit "be-ven bakar", :gloss "regarding cattle"} {:he "מנחת הדל", :translit "minchat ha-dal", :gloss "meal-offering of the poor"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrasts 'before YHWH' absent from bird- and meal-offerings vs. present in cattle-offerings; poor person's shame motivates the difference"}], :frame {:text "The word 'nefesh' in connection with a meal-offering is explained midrashically: since the poor person has little, his offering costs him his very soul. Leviticus Rabbah 3:5 records that the Holy One says of the poor man's offering, 'I account it as though he offered his soul before Me.' Menahot 104b-105a discusses why bird-offerings and meal-offerings lack the phrase 'before the Lord' found in cattle-offerings (Leviticus 1:3), attributing it to the shame of the poor. Menahot 104b further derives from the word 'lecha' addressed to Aaron that the kohen must not despise the meal-offering of the poor.", :sources ["Leviticus Rabbah 3:5" "Menahot 104b" "Menahot 105a" "Leviticus 1:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrasts 'before YHWH' absent from bird- and meal-offerings vs. present in cattle-offerings; poor person's shame motivates the difference", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:21:51.503410608Z", :model "glm-5.2"}